      "math_academy_id": "e-14302",
      "problem": "Simplify the polynomial $3x^2-2-4x - 6x^2+18,$ giving your final answer in standard form.",
      "worked_solution": "First, we collect like terms:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}-2-4x-6{x}^{2}+18 & = \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2}-2+18-4x & = \\\\ (3{x}^{2}-6{x}^{2})+(-2+18)-4x & = \\\\ (3-6){x}^{2}+(-2+18)-4x & = \\\\ -3{x}^{2}+16-4x & \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to express our polynomial in standard form. \n\nThe highest exponent term is $-3x^2,$ followed by $-4x,$ and finally $16.$\n\nSo, the standard form of the polynomial is\n\n$$\n-3x^2-4x+16.\n$$",
